<article class="env-definition" id="07BN">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/07BN">Definition <span data-tag="07BN">10.134.1</span>.</a> Let $R \to S$ be a ring map. The <em>naive cotangent complex</em> $\mathop{N\! L}\nolimits _{S/R}$ is the chain complex (<a href="/tag/07BM" data-tag="07BM">10.134.0.2</a>) </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \mathop{N\! L}\nolimits _{S/R} = \left(I/I^2 \longrightarrow \Omega _{R[S]/R} \otimes _{R[S]} S\right)  \]
</div>
  <p> with $I/I^2$ placed in (homological) degree $1$ and $\Omega _{R[S]/R} \otimes _{R[S]} S$ placed in degree $0$. We will denote $H_1(L_{S/R}) = H_1(\mathop{N\! L}\nolimits _{S/R})$<a class="footnotemark" href="#a0000194971" id="a0000194971-mark"><sup>1</sup></a> the homology in degree $1$. </p>
</article>